-- title:
--   Local chart presentation at a node of the resolved model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and a package $\mathfrak X$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data for the full level-$p$ modular curve over $\mathbb Z$; let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved-model package for these data, with node set, width function $w$, component ideal sheaves indexed by `X0MqComponents`, and a proper map $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ to $\mathcal X_O := \mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{DRModel.toBase}\,p,\ \mathrm{Spec}\,O)$. Let $Fc$ assign to each $e$ and each $i \in \mathrm{Fin}(e+1)$ an ideal sheaf on the chain resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}\,p\,e$, subject to $hF$: on the $i$-th standard chart, $Fc\,e\,k'$ pulls back to the ideal generated by $V$ if $k'=i$, by $U$ if $k'=i+1$, and to the unit ideal otherwise. Let $ch$ be a system of étale crossing charts for $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ relative to $\varpi=p$ and $Fc$, and let $n$ be a node. Then, writing $x_n$ for the image in $\mathcal X_O$ of the point $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{nodeEquiv}\,n$ of the intersection of the two characteristic-$p$ components, there are specialisation relations $h_\infty$, $h_0$ from the images of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under the $\infty$-component map and the $0$-component map (each composed with base change along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$) to $x_n$, and there are elements $u,v,w_0$ of the stalk $R$ of $\mathcal X_O$ at $x_n$ such that $w_0$ is a unit, $uv = p^{w(n)}w_0$, $(p,u,v)$ is the maximal ideal of $R$, $(p,u)$ is the contraction along the specialisation map $\mathrm{stalkSpecializes}\,h_\infty$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk at the $\infty$-branch generic point, $(p,v)$ is likewise the contraction along $\mathrm{stalkSpecializes}\,h_0$, and moreover for every section $t : \mathrm{Spec}\,O \to \mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.Y$ of $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}$ whose composite with $\mathrm{toDR}$ sends the closed point of $O$ to $x_n$, and every $d \in \mathbb N$: if the additive valuation of $O$ of the image of $v$ under the induced map on stalks at the closed point equals $d$, then for every index $c$ the closed point of $O$ lands under $t$ in the support of the component ideal sheaf $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,c$ precisely when $c = \mathrm{chainPos}\,w\,n\,d$, i.e. $c$ is the first end component if $d=0$, the $(d-1)$-st exceptional component of the chain over $n$ if $0<d<w(n)$, and the second end component otherwise.
--
--   This is the formal counterpart of the Deligne–Rapoport local description of the modular curve at a supersingular point, $uv = p^{e}$ with $e$ the width, together with the identification of the two branches and of the chain position of an $O$-valued section by the valuation of $v$. It packages the local data in the exact shape required by [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts) and [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.width_eq_jWidth_of_exists_jFun_sub_mem_maximalIdeal_of_prolongationTuple`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.width_eq_jWidth_of_exists_jFun_sub_mem_maximalIdeal_of_prolongationTuple).
